{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787977410051617001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"beribboned-enstatite-hoopoe","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"ad9ca8432a09619a790c38e4b3ad7a7fc00f680287dc1a9ae1c27132b56d824d","event_uuid":"831412ad-d2d5-4e9e-bfa9-f37f82b336a7","position":{"commit_sha":"1200d6fabee05c3acb3501402410f831b6632854","position":"1787973707109523001-831412ad-d2d5-4e9e-bfa9-f37f82b336a7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bc6cafa9d3d5a255dae236c4e7f63cd88c32def98345c3d8b3333b526925a242","event_uuid":"442caf8e-1aaf-4d6e-9085-f3b0f728e176","position":{"commit_sha":"e53193e0b20bf88d31863912497a0aeae5c24cdf","position":"1787973720831028001-442caf8e-1aaf-4d6e-9085-f3b0f728e176"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787973707109523001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"442caf8e-1aaf-4d6e-9085-f3b0f728e176","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"56b7-b21a-c8ab-4afc"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nPinning uv (bug 56b7-b21a-c8ab-4afc) removed the VERSION-RESOLUTION manifest fetch, but CI still makes one network call to `raw.githubusercontent.com` per job, so the `##[error]fetch failed` failure mode that killed run 33214025855 is still reachable.\n\nVerified on run 33230196661 (change 2367 patchset 1), five jobs sampled, all identical:\n\n    Found version for uv in /home/runner/work/rebar/rebar/pyproject.toml: 0.12.7\n    Fetching manifest data from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astral-sh/versions/main/v1/uv.ndjson ...\n    Successfully installed uv version 0.12.7\n\nThe version came from the local pin — no `Could not determine uv version` line — and the manifest was fetched anyway.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`setup-uv` has a SECOND, independent manifest consumer. `setupUv` (`src/setup-uv.ts`) calls `tryGetFromToolCache`; on a miss it calls `downloadVersion`, whose first statement is:\n\n    const artifact = await getArtifact(version, arch, platform, manifestUrl);   // src/download/download-version.ts:42\n\nThe manifest supplies the download URL and sha256, so it is fetched unconditionally regardless of how the version was resolved. A GitHub-hosted runner starts each job with an empty uv tool cache, so the miss is guaranteed. This is unchanged in v10.0.1, the newest release. A committed local manifest does not help: `fetchManifestResponse` uses Node `fetch()`, which rejects `file:` URLs, and `manifest-file` is documented as a URL.\n\n## Candidate approaches (choose ONE during planning; none is pre-selected here)\n\n- Restore the uv binary into the runner tool cache with `actions/cache` keyed on the pinned version, so `tryGetFromToolCache` hits and `downloadVersion` never runs. Trades a raw.githubusercontent.com dependency for a GitHub-cache-service dependency, which is a different and better-instrumented failure domain — but it is still a network dependency, so state that honestly rather than claiming zero.\n- Install uv without the action (direct download from `releases.astral.sh` at the pinned version with a committed sha256, mirroring the `acli` precedent in `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`). Removes the manifest entirely; costs the action's caching and PATH wiring, which would have to be reimplemented at 25 call sites or in one composite action.\n- Upstream a change to `astral-sh/setup-uv` that skips `getArtifact` when the version is exact and the checksum is already in `KNOWN_CHECKSUMS`, then bump the pin.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A real CI log for the change contains the liveness anchor `Successfully installed uv version <pinned>` AND zero occurrences of `Fetching manifest data`; both greps recorded verbatim on this ticket. The anchor is asserted FIRST — a zero-match grep alone is also produced by an empty log or a skipped step, which is how an empty `gh run view --job=N --log` scored a clean vacuous pass during 56b7's verification.\n- [ ] The installed uv version in that same log still equals the pin in `pyproject.toml`, so the fix does not silently change which uv runs.\n- [ ] Whatever residual network dependency the chosen approach retains is named explicitly in the change description; the change does not claim 'no network dependency' unless the log shows zero external fetches in the install path.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5caa-4b63-7ea2-4e71","ticket_type":"bug","title":"setup-uv fetches the version manifest for the artifact URL on every job even when uv is pinned","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["831412ad-d2d5-4e9e-bfa9-f37f82b336a7","442caf8e-1aaf-4d6e-9085-f3b0f728e176"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787977410051617001,"uuid":"3bb07711-991c-42c8-a6ef-2d8b1ba0e8ad"}